Cline task guardrails:
- Obey the task's total time limit and named stop-coding point.
- Before the final focused test, run `cargo fmt --all` once.
- Run the requested final test/check once. Do not repeat equivalent commands after a pass or failure.
- If blocked, report the blocker rather than trying a second design.
- Always report elapsed time, whether the limit was met, changed files, and test result.
- Do not stage, commit, push, or touch `cline-kimi-loop-evidence-2026-07-17-18/` unless explicitly instructed.

## Rust

- The repository toolchain is Rust 1.98.1 (Edition 2024). Do not use features or APIs introduced after the pinned toolchain.
- Read `docs/RUST_GUIDE_FOR_AGENTS.md` before editing `.rs`, `Cargo.toml`, or `Cargo.lock`.
- No new dependencies or feature changes without explicit task approval.
- Respect crate boundaries: `lighting-core` has no I/O; SurrealDB stays behind repository traits.
- No `unwrap()` or `expect()` in production integration paths.
- Do not block async worker threads with synchronous I/O.
- Run `cargo fmt --all` before the final test.
- `Cargo.lock` is authoritative for dependency resolution.
